<title>INDIA: India Tata Tea gains for second day.</title>
<headline>India Tata Tea gains for second day.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of India's Tata Tea rose 14.50 rupees, or 4.3 percent to 353.25, a new 52-week high at the Bombay exchange on Friday as local players bought into the stock after the firm posted higher than expected 1996/97 profits, traders said.</p>
<p>Tata Tea on Wednesday announced a net profit of 586.2 million rupees for the year ending March 31, 1997 from 460.8 million last year. The firm set a higher dividend of 6.5 rupees per share from 6.0 rupees in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Tata Tea jumped nearly six percent on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Bombay equities desk +91-22-265 9000</p>
